libfprint-egis0576-tod (0.4.4) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Dropped the "-1" revision. debian/source/format is 3.0 (native), and a
    native package's version must carry no Debian revision at all: with one,
    lintian's source-format check flags it as an error on the very
    dpkg-buildpackage -S build the PPA path relies on. Kept 3.0 (native)
    rather than moving to 3.0 (quilt), since this package carries no
    debian/patches of its own (the meson integration lives entirely in
    ../meson.build, not a patch). build-series.sh's per-series ~24.04 /
    ~26.04 suffix still applies on top of this bare version.
  * debian/copyright: fixed a false statement at the old line 47 saying
    this package carries no PROVENANCE.md category 3 files and none of
    tsteppy/egis_match.{c,h}. That is true of the built binary (only the
    vendor matcher is linked), but false of the SOURCE package:
    build-series.sh stages extra-driver with cp -rL, which dereferences the
    ../../driver symlink into real files, so dpkg-buildpackage -S carries
    the whole of driver/ regardless of which matcher ../meson.build
    compiles. Added a Files stanza for extra-driver/egis0576/tsteppy/* under
    Thaddeus Stepanovich's copyright and LGPL-2.1-or-later, added
    extra-driver/egis0576/egis_engine_cleanroom.c to the category 1 stanza,
    and added a Files: * fallback. Copyright lines taken from
    PROVENANCE.md and the files' own headers, not invented.
  * debian/rules: install the two integration files v0.4.5 added
    (egis0576-fp-wait and its fprintd.service.d drop-in) alongside the
    sleep hook and udev rule already installed, mirroring
    packaging/fedora/libfprint.spec and packaging/debian/rules. Before this
    the package shipped the sleep hook's /run marker with nothing that
    consumed it.
  * postinst: udevadm trigger now passes --action=add, matching
    integration/60-egis0576-fp-nosuspend.rules' ACTION=="add" match. The
    previous default (--action=change) never matched that rule, so the
    already-enumerated sensor at install time never got the no-autosuspend
    rule applied until the next reboot -- exactly the case the postinst
    exists for.
  * debian/control: Maintainer set to Irving Popovetsky
    <libfprint-egis0576@popovetsky.com>, matching packaging/debian/control.
    The previous users.noreply.github.com address is well formed but not a
    working mailbox, and this field is shown by apt show and used by
    Launchpad to mail PPA build failures.

 -- Irving Popovetsky <libfprint-egis0576@popovetsky.com>  Mon, 15 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
